{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4kEF2q7MJNdz98cHck","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient oak, iron-banded, silent.*\n\n*A keyhole glints dully in the dim light.*\n\n*You said \"key.\" But you hold nothing. The lock does not turn.*\n\n*I remain closed.*\n\n*Present the right key, and I will open. But a word alone is not a key — it is only the name of one.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":87,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}